    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but \"structural shift\" sounds pretty certain. some analysts are pointing to the massive issues with grid stability and the sheer difficulty of scaling mineral supply chains for batteries. if those things hit a wall, wouldn't that turn the \"inevitability\" into a massive economic miscalculation for anyone heavily invested in green tech right now?",
