      "content": "it just feels like you're framing the \"move away from fossil fuels\" as the inevitable end state regardless of what happens with the tech or the economy. if the costs of maintaining a stable grid with renewables end up being orders of magnitude higher than stickng with traditional baseload, wouldn't that make the whole \"inevitability\" argument a bit of a false consensus?",
